 "equipment_type": "Boiler",
 "applies_to": "Buderus SSB series condensing boilers (Bosch Thermotechnology, North America) using the Modbus terminals on the boiler's internal terminal strip, per installation instructions 6720818450 (2015/10).",
 "summary": "Buderus SSB floor-standing condensing boilers have a Modbus RTU slave on their own controller. Everything is a 16-bit holding register: burner state, status and error code, pump outputs, supply/return/DHW/flue temperatures, firing rate, counters, lockout and blocking history, cascade dependents, and the CH, DHW and outdoor-reset setpoints. Writes need a write-enable bit set just before each write.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 2,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "The document prints decimal register numbers with their hex form (98 = 0x0062) and says to use them as printed when the master counts from 0x0000, and to add 1 only if the master counts from 0x0001. So register 100 is wire address 100."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Modbus for Buderus SSB Boilers - Installation and Service Instructions for Contractors",
  "doc_number": "6720818450 (2015/10) US Rev.0",
  "revision_date": "2015-10",
  "url": "https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/service/technical_guides/6720818450_ssb_boiler_modbus_installation_instructions_en_10.2015_us_us.pdf",
  "pages": "p. 4 (wiring, serial settings, addressing), pp. 5-7 (register tables), p. 8 (control register, write enable, unit selection, data types), pp. 9-11 (state, status, error tables)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Scaling follows the document's data-type table: temperatures, pressures, voltages, flame current and percentages are sent x10 (one decimal). Registers marked 'automatic conversion' use it; state, status and error codes and the counters do not.",
  "Temperatures follow the unit chosen in register 98 (°C or °F) for both reads and writes; the document does not say which bit value means which unit or what the default is, so check a known reading first.",
  "The document never says whether values are signed. Outside temperature (125) and the outdoor reset-curve points (506 Outdoor Mild Weather, 507 Outdoor Design) can be below zero, so they are left out rather than guessed; the other temperatures are typed unsigned.",
  "Left out: successful ignition counter 200 (printed with 'resolution 16', meaning not explained); CH mode 500 and DHW mode 501 (range '0..x' with no value list).",
  "Only the first slot of the lockout and blocking histories is listed; slots 2-16 follow at consecutive addresses (lockouts 221-235, blockings 261-275). The history is not in order of occurrence.",
  "Dependent registers 300-339 report the cascade dependents (01-07) in the same state/error code tables; the document leaves their access column blank, so they are listed read-only.",
  "Left out: the 'time after lockout' (236-251) and 'time after blocking' (276-291) hour stamps. They are marked 'automatic conversion' yet hours are not one of the x10 data types in the document's data-type table, so their scaling is unclear; the burn-hour counters 203-204 carry no such mark."
 ],
